But when someone says "everybody hates me" they usually don't mean to
include themselves, or people who have never heard of them. There's
usually some implicit restriction involved in the context: "everybody
relevant to what I'm saying". Not every person who has ever lived, or
ever will live or ever could live, or imaginary persons, or persons
that perhaps exist in another planet, or... So if you think that "ro
da" is bad because it is too general, then "ro prenu" is just as bad,
since a mere restriction to people is nowhere near enough.

